From da19e3ef5824c8fe95d1cb38d868c7195b7a128b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:09:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/28] WIP mmb: RDNA4 (gfx12) fragment port + the arch-scoped
 weight-type/path split

Ported to RDNA4 (S5-S7, 2026-09-21): one arch-selected shim (gfx12 8-half "two
runs of four" A/B + accumulator m = 8*hi + e + the _gfx12 builtins; gfx11 keeps
the 16-half row and m = 2*e + hi) at 7 sites, and mmb_enabled() accepts RDNA4.
The gfx11 arm is a MACRO, not a __device__ function: a function left a dead
`lane >> 4` argument that perturbed the scheduler and broke codegen identity
(the gfx11 device asm is now byte-identical but for the __hip_cuid_* symbol,
opcode histogram md5 equal).

The switch was then SPLIT, because measurement says mmb is not a blanket win:
  - un-scoped (all types, dense path on) it is a -4..-13 % prefill regression
  - wins are confined to the routed-MoE path and the qwen4exp HC paths
  - the generic quantized dense tile GEMM loses for every type measured
  - a 27B UD-IQ3_S (82 % IQ, dense) losing -3 % proves the path matters as much
    as the weight type
So:
  - mmb_wtype_ok()/mmb_wtype_mask(): ONE arch-scoped weight-type policy,
    replacing five duplicated hard-coded copies (which had drifted).  RDNA4 =
    the IQ family; RDNA3_5/RDNA3_0 keep the full set (gfx1151 unchanged).
    GGML_CUDA_MMB_TYPES=<csv> overrides.
  - mmb_dense_flag(): separates the generic dense tile GEMM + the F32 router
    (the losers) from the routed/HC paths (the winners).  RDNA4 default: off.
    GGML_CUDA_MMB_DENSE=0|1 overrides.
  - mmb_tall_shape(): keeps the qwen4exp HC tall-M tile out of the dense
    stand-down (otherwise the dense flag silently kills the HC win).

The graph's MMQ-fusion stand-down goes through these same predicates, so an
excluded type/path costs nothing.  Net with the scoped default: neutral
wherever it would lose, +3..+7 % where it wins.  Correctness: PPL parity
(7 chunks, 12.7378 vs 12.7221; fast model 14.3981 vs 14.4087).
Matrix: wip/mmb-general/gfx1201-s5s7-mmb-results.md.
